      "text": "To determine the number with the greatest number of divisors among the numbers 1, 2, 3, ..., 15, we first need to find the prime factorization of each number in that range.\n\nFor example, the prime factorization of 1 is 1, since 1 is not a product of prime numbers.\n\nThe prime factorization of 2 is 2, since 2 is a prime number.\n\nThe prime factorization of 3 is 3, since 3 is a prime number.\n\nThe prime factorization of 4 is 2^2, since 4 can be written as 2 x 2.\n\nThe prime factorization of 5 is 5, since 5 is a prime number.\n\nThe prime factorization of 6 is 2 x 3, since 6 can be written as 2 x 3.\n\nThe prime factorization of 7 is 7, since 7 is a prime number.\n\nThe prime factorization of 8 is 2^3, since 8 can be written as 2 x 2 x 2.\n\nThe prime factorization of 9 is 3^2, since 9 can be written as 3 x 3.\n\nThe prime factorization of 10 is 2 x 5, since 10 can be written as 2 x 5.\n\nThe prime factorization of 11 is 11, since 11 is a prime number.\n\nThe prime factorization of 12 is 2^2 x 3, since 12 can be written as 2 x 2 x 3.\n\nThe prime factorization of 13 is 13, since 13 is a prime number.\n\nThe prime factorization of 14 is 2 x 7, since 14 can be written as 2 x 7.\n\nThe prime factorization of 15 is 3 x 5, since 15 can be written as 3 x 5.\n\nNext, we count the number of divisors for each number. For example, the number 1 has 1 factor (1), 2 has 2 factors (1, 2), 3 has 2 factors (1, 3), and so on.\n\nCounting the number of factors for the first five numbers, we get 1, 2, 2, 3, 2, respectively. To find the number of divisors for each of the remaining numbers, we can look at their prime factorizations. For example, 4 has the prime factorization of 2^2, so it has 3 factors (1, 2, and 4). Similarly, 8 has the prime factorization of 2^3, so it has 4 factors (1, 2, 4, and 8). The same works for 9, which has the prime factorization of 3^2, so it has 3 factors (1, 3, and 9).\n\nUsing these calculations, we can determine that the number with the greatest number of divisors is 12, which has the prime factorization of 2^2 x 3.\n\nTherefore, the answer is 12.",
